## Analysis

My approach:

1. **Null/empty guard** — return a freshly-constructed `ImportResult` (constructor initializes all members non-null).
2. **Pre-pass (no DML)** — walk input in order, normalize each email (trim + lowercase; blank → treated as "no email"). The first lead for a normalized email is registered in a `Set` and kept for insert; any later lead with the same email gets the duplicate error and is **not** added to the insert list. Because the email is registered during the pre-pass, duplicates are flagged even if the first lead later fails the DB insert.
3. **LeadSource default** — set to `Web` only on leads actually being inserted, when blank.
4. **Single DML** — one `Database.insert(list, false)` (allOrNone=false → partial success, never throws for invalid rows). Guard against the empty-list exception.
5. **Result assembly** — map each `SaveResult` back to its original input index; successes append Id and bump count (naturally input order); failures join `getMessage()` values with `; `.
6. **Sharing** — declare `with sharing` so the DML respects the running user.

`File: force-app/main/default/classes/LeadImportService.cls`

```apex
public with sharing class LeadImportService {

    /**
     * Result of a lead import operation.
     * All members are initialized to non-null values in the constructor.
     */
    public class ImportResult {
        public Integer successCount { get; set; }
        public List<Id> insertedIds { get; set; }
        public Map<Integer, String> errorsByIndex { get; set; }

        public ImportResult() {
            successCount = 0;
            insertedIds = new List<Id>();
            errorsByIndex = new Map<Integer, String>();
        }
    }

    /**
     * Imports a list of leads, inserting every lead that can be inserted and
     * collecting per-row errors without ever throwing for invalid input.
     *
     * @param leads Leads to import (input order is preserved in the results)
     * @return ImportResult with success count, inserted Ids, and per-index errors
     */
    public static LeadImportService.ImportResult importLeads(List<Lead> leads) {
        ImportResult result = new ImportResult();

        if (leads == null || leads.isEmpty()) {
            return result;
        }

        Set<String> seenEmails = new Set<String>();
        List<Lead> leadsToInsert = new List<Lead>();
        Map<Integer, Integer> insertToInputIndex = new Map<Integer, Integer>();

        // Pre-pass: resolve duplicates (by normalized email) and default LeadSource.
        // No DML happens here, so the "first" occurrence is fixed by input order
        // regardless of whether it later succeeds or fails the database insert.
        for (Integer i = 0; i < leads.size(); i++) {
            Lead lead = leads[i];
            if (lead == null) {
                continue;
            }

            String normalizedEmail = normalizeEmail(lead.Email);
            if (normalizedEmail != null && !seenEmails.add(normalizedEmail)) {
                // A lead with this email already appeared earlier in the call.
                result.errorsByIndex.put(i, 'Duplicate email in import: ' + normalizedEmail);
                continue;
            }

            if (String.isBlank(lead.LeadSource)) {
                lead.LeadSource = 'Web';
            }

            insertToInputIndex.put(leadsToInsert.size(), i);
            leadsToInsert.add(lead);
        }

        // Single DML statement; allOrNone=false so valid rows still insert.
        if (!leadsToInsert.isEmpty()) {
            Database.SaveResult[] saveResults = Database.insert(leadsToInsert, false);

            for (Integer j = 0; j < saveResults.size(); j++) {
                Database.SaveResult sr = saveResults[j];
                Integer inputIndex = insertToInputIndex.get(j);

                if (sr.isSuccess()) {
                    result.insertedIds.add(sr.getId());
                    result.successCount++;
                } else {
                    List<String> messages = new List<String>();
                    for (Database.Error de : sr.getErrors()) {
                        messages.add(de.getMessage());
                    }
                    result.errorsByIndex.put(inputIndex, String.join(messages, '; '));
                }
            }
        }

        return result;
    }

    /**
     * Normalizes an email for duplicate comparison: trims surrounding
     * whitespace and lower-cases it. Returns null when there is no usable
     * address, so leads without an email are never treated as duplicates.
     */
    private static String normalizeEmail(String email) {
        if (email == null) {
            return null;
        }
        String normalized = email.trim().toLowerCase();
        return normalized == '' ? null : normalized;
    }
}
