## Reasoning

The requirement is **all-or-nothing**, which rules out the plain `/composite` endpoint — each of its subrequests commits in its own transaction, so a later failure wouldn't roll back earlier saves.

The **Composite Graph** endpoint (`/composite/graph`) with `atomic: true` runs every subrequest in a **single transaction**: if any fails, everything rolls back. It also executes subrequests **in order within that one transaction**, so the Asset is already inserted (and thus queryable) by the time the `Service_Request__c` is inserted — satisfying the before-insert trigger's SOQL lookup on `Asset.SerialNumber`.

I place all three subrequests in `graph.requests` in the required order, reference the Account's Id into the Asset via `{"!newAccount":"Id"}`, and set `Serial_Number__c` directly on the service request.

