## Analysis

The plan:

1. **`TA_Contact_Queries`** – a per‑transaction singleton (private constructor, static `getInstance()`) exposing `public Map<Id, Account> accountsById`. Its inner `public class Service` implements `TriggerAction.BeforeInsert`, collects the `AccountId`s from the batch and runs **one** SOQL query into the shared map, reloading on every execution. Querying the Billing fields **and** `AccountSource` covers both follow‑up actions.
2. **`TA_Contact_InheritMailingAddress`** / **`TA_Contact_DefaultLeadSource`** – implement `TriggerAction.BeforeInsert`, read the shared map (no queries of their own), and only touch Contacts that have an Account.
3. Three `Trigger_Action__mdt` records registered for **Before Insert** (via the `Before_Insert__c` MetadataRelationship → the `Contact` `sObject_Trigger_Setting__mdt` record), ordered 1 / 10 / 20, each with a `Description__c`.

Only the Service queries; both actions read `TA_Contact_Queries.getInstance().accountsById`, giving exactly one Account query per trigger execution shared by both.

---

File: force-app/main/default/classes/TA_Contact_Queries.cls
```apex
public class TA_Contact_Queries {

    // Singleton: one instance per transaction. Private constructor prevents
    // direct instantiation; use getInstance().
    private TA_Contact_Queries() {
    }

    private static TA_Contact_Queries instance;

    // Parent Accounts for the current trigger execution, shared by every action.
    // Initialized non-null so readers never hit an NPE.
    public Map<Id, Account> accountsById = new Map<Id, Account>();

    public static TA_Contact_Queries getInstance() {
        if (instance == null) {
            instance = new TA_Contact_Queries();
        }
        return instance;
    }

    // The trigger action (runs first, Order__c = 1). Loads the parent Accounts
    // of this insert batch exactly once and reloads them on every execution,
    // because later DML in the same transaction can involve other Accounts.
    public class Service implements TriggerAction.BeforeInsert {
        public void beforeInsert(List<SObject> triggerNew) {
            Set<Id> accountIds = new Set<Id>();
            for (Contact c : triggerNew) {
                if (c.AccountId != null) {
                    accountIds.add(c.AccountId);
                }
            }

            Map<Id, Account> accounts = new Map<Id, Account>();
            if (!accountIds.isEmpty()) {
                accounts = new Map<Id, Account>([
                    SELECT Id,
                           BillingStreet,
                           BillingCity,
                           BillingPostalCode,
                           BillingCountry,
                           AccountSource
                    FROM Account
                    WHERE Id IN :accountIds
                ]);
            }

            TA_Contact_Queries.getInstance().accountsById = accounts;
        }
    }
}
```

